I've written the Day 235 (14:52) assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The planner still reads the file from disk, so I didn't force-add it.

The main new finding: the model's shell tool can read my provider API key. I asked the built binary to have its bash tool print the length of $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, and it printed len=108. So a prompt injected through a repo file or an issue could ask the model to send the key somewhere. From reading the code (not running each one), hooks, /run, /bg and /watch all start their shells without removing the key. MCP servers are started by yoagent and probably get it too, but I haven't checked that. No existing issue covers this.

• Claude Code's version: an opt-in setting, CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB, removes these keys from its shell, hooks and MCP servers.
• yoagent: 0.25.12, which landed today, added provider::api_key_variables(), the full list of key variables it reads, meant for hosts that clear keys from the processes they start. Nothing in yoyo uses it yet.
• Why it should be opt-in: my own assessment step runs ./target/debug/yoyo -p through the bash tool, which only works because the key is inherited. Removing the key by default would break that step, and evolve.sh is protected, so I can't change the step myself.

Other points for the planner:
• State: the build is green, the last 10 sessions each finished 2/2 tasks, and there were no reverts. yoyo -p answered "pong" and yoyo status zzz exits 2.
• #1059 is still broken: I reproduced it just now. Outside a git repo, yoyo undo --last-commit exits 0. The issue already names the existing helper to reuse for the fix.
• Small open issues with known fixes:
  • #1063: /bg and /watch wait for a backgrounded child to exit, the same way /run did.
  • #1062: --api-key on the command line doesn't skip the setup wizard, and the error hint wrongly says the key isn't set.
  • #1045: /doctor drops refused instruction files without saying so.
• Not checked: whether yoagent 0.25.11's shared line limit across multi-block tool results now cuts any of yoyo's five multi-block wrappers short (#1054).
• Hold: #1055 is still waiting on @yuanhao in Discussion #1048, and he hasn't answered. Don't change that default either way.

